---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% from "components/macros.njk" import metric, chip, kicker %}

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO — an experiment currently running
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="hero container">
  <div class="hero-main" data-reveal>
    <p class="kicker">
      <span class="kicker-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Deep Q-Learning · in-browser reinforcement learning
    </p>
    <h1>Teaching an agent<br>to play Flappy&nbsp;Bird.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A continuous learning experiment. A neural network plays, crashes, stores the
      experience, updates itself, and tries again — every frame, entirely in the browser.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/how-it-works/' | url }}">How it works</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ '/demo/' | url }}">Watch the agent</a>
      <a class="btn btn--text" href="{{ site.repo }}" rel="noopener">View source&nbsp;↗</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="hero-stack" aria-label="Technology stack">
      <li>Phaser 3.90</li>
      <li>TensorFlow.js 4.22</li>
      <li>DQN</li>
      <li>IndexedDB persistence</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-panel" data-reveal>
    <div class="panel hero-instrument">
      <p class="panel-label-row">
        <span class="panel-label">Fig. 01 — the environment the agent sees</span>
        <span class="panel-label panel-label--dim">live in <a href="{{ '/demo/' | url }}">demo</a></span>
      </p>
      {% set caption = "" %}
      {% include "components/game-figure.njk" %}
      {% include "components/agent-status.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     DATA FLOW STRIP
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container hero-strip" aria-label="The learning data flow" data-reveal>
  {% include "components/pipeline-strip.njk" %}
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     WHAT IS THIS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <header class="home-section-head" data-reveal>
    {{ kicker("01 · The project") }}
    <h2>A game, an agent,<br>and a public lab notebook.</h2>
    <p class="home-section-lede">
      DQN Flappy Bird is a personal research experiment in reinforcement learning.
      It is not finished — that is the point. The site documents the agent as it evolves.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="card-grid card-grid--3">
    <article class="card" data-reveal>
      <span class="card-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <h3>The game</h3>
      <p>
        A Flappy Bird environment built with Phaser 3: gravity, pipes, and one brutal rule —
        touch anything and the episode ends. Pipe speed grows with the score,
        so success literally makes the world faster.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card" data-reveal>
      <span class="card-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <h3>The agent</h3>
      <p>
        A Deep Q-Network running on TensorFlow.js. It sees 8 normalized numbers,
        outputs two Q-values — <em>idle</em> or <em>flap</em> — and acts once per frame.
        Roughly {{ impl.network.totalParams | num }} parameters, no discretization.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card" data-reveal>
      <span class="card-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <h3>The experiment</h3>
      <p>
        Training never really ends. Every change — a reward tweak, a new state variable,
        a different sampling strategy — becomes a numbered, documented experiment
        with its own configuration, results, and Git tag.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="section-more" data-reveal><a href="{{ '/project/' | url }}">Read about the project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     HOW THE AGENT LEARNS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <div class="split">
    <div class="split-copy" data-reveal>
      {{ kicker("02 · How it works") }}
      <h2>State in. Action out.<br>Reward closes the loop.</h2>
      <p>
        Once per frame the environment hands the agent an 8-value state — distances,
        velocity, gap geometry, world speed. The network answers with two Q-values,
        the agent picks the better action, and the resulting reward is stored as
        experience. Batches of that experience train the network against the Bellman target.
      </p>
      <p>
        On death the brain is saved to IndexedDB and a new generation starts
        automatically — the agent keeps training across browser sessions.
      </p>
      <p class="section-more"><a href="{{ '/how-it-works/' | url }}">The full mechanism <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-figure" data-reveal>
      {% include "components/loop-diagram.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     THE NETWORK
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <div class="split split--flip">
    <div class="split-copy" data-reveal>
      {{ kicker("03 · The network") }}
      <h2>Eight numbers in.<br>Two Q-values out.</h2>
      <p>
        The policy network is a fully-connected stack —
        <strong>8 → 512 → 256 → 128 → 64 → 2</strong> — trained with Adam on mean-squared
        error. A frozen target network, synced every {{ impl.training.targetUpdateFreq | num }} steps,
        keeps the bootstrapped targets stable.
      </p>
      <div class="chip-row" role="list" aria-label="Network facts">
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">{{ impl.network.totalParams | num }} params</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">ReLU × 4</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">Adam · lr {{ impl.training.learningRate }}</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">γ = {{ impl.training.gamma }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="section-more"><a href="{{ '/how-it-works/neural-network/' | url }}">Network details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-figure" data-reveal>
      {% include "components/nn-canvas.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     TRAINING
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <div class="split">
    <div class="split-copy" data-reveal>
      {{ kicker("04 · Training") }}
      <h2>Exploration decays.<br>Experience accumulates.</h2>
      <p>
        The agent starts curious — ε = {{ impl.training.epsilonStart }}, mostly random
        (but flap-biased) actions — and anneals toward pure exploitation.
        Every transition feeds a {{ (impl.memory.legacySize / 1000) | round }}k-transition replay memory,
        sampled in batches of {{ impl.training.batchSize }} every {{ impl.training.trainThrottle }} steps.
      </p>
      <div class="chip-row" role="list" aria-label="Training hyperparameters">
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">ε {{ impl.training.epsilonStart }} → {{ impl.training.epsilonMin }}</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">decay {{ impl.training.epsilonDecay }}</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">batch {{ impl.training.batchSize }}</span>
        <span class="chip" role="listitem">target sync {{ impl.training.targetUpdateFreq | num }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="section-more"><a href="{{ '/training/' | url }}">Inside the training loop <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-figure" data-reveal>
      {% set caption = "Epsilon schedule, computed from the real constants in src/rl/dqn.js." %}
      {% include "components/epsilon-chart.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     EXPERIMENTS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <header class="home-section-head home-section-head--row" data-reveal>
    <div>
      {{ kicker("05 · Experiments") }}
      <h2>Every change is an experiment.</h2>
      <p class="home-section-lede">
        Hypothesis, configuration, results, conclusion — numbered, versioned, and compared.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="section-more"><a href="{{ '/experiments/' | url }}">All experiments <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </header>

  {% if experiments.usingDemo %}
  <aside class="placeholder-note" role="note" data-reveal>
    <span class="placeholder-note-badge">placeholder</span>
    <p>No experiments have been published to <code>experiments/</code> yet — the cards below preview the interface with illustrative data.</p>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="card-grid card-grid--2">
    {% for exp in experiments.recent %}
    <div data-reveal>{% include "components/experiment-card.njk" %}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     INSIGHTS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal-root>
  <header class="home-section-head home-section-head--row" data-reveal>
    <div>
      {{ kicker("06 · Insights") }}
      <h2>The knowledge base behind the agent.</h2>
      <p class="home-section-lede">
        Techniques, observations, and papers that shape what gets tried next.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="section-more"><a href="{{ '/insights/' | url }}">All insights <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </header>

  <div class="card-grid card-grid--3">
    {% for post in collections.insights | slice(0, 3) %}
    <div data-reveal>{% include "components/insight-card.njk" %}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     DEMO CTA
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="container home-section" data-reveal>
  <div class="demo-cta panel">
    <div class="demo-cta-copy">
      <p class="kicker kicker--light"><span class="kicker-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>07 · Live demo</p>
      <h2>Watch the agent learn — live.</h2>
      <p>
        The demo is the real thing: the same Phaser game and the same DQN agent from
        this repository, training itself in your browser tab. Progress persists locally —
        come back later and the agent remembers.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--light" href="{{ '/demo/' | url }}">Open the live demo</a>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-cta-meta" aria-label="Demo details">
      <p><span class="demo-meta-label">RUNS</span> entirely client-side</p>
      <p><span class="demo-meta-label">PERSISTS</span> IndexedDB · your browser</p>
      <p><span class="demo-meta-label">SOURCE</span> <a href="{{ site.repo }}" rel="noopener">github.com/danrosselli/dqn-flappy-bird</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
